ecute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA2","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":43,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]},{"category":"Output Handling","code_snippet":"\n## Throttle high-volume exception reports\n\nA failing integration can flood logs or error tracking. Configure `throttle()` with a `Lottery` or `Limit` result to sample or rate-limit matching exception reports. Choose keys deliberately when separate exception classes, tenants, or integrations need independent limits.\n\n## Prevent duplicate reports of one exception instance\n","confidence":0.8,"evidence":{},"finding":"flood log","finding_ids":["finding-a21ec5de7a2d4e708baafa634fd3b503"],"id":"sha256:5dbdc42a4a3284d1916309226b1b6e5cf9986ea595df437d77c12e632d10cbb5","intent":null,"line":49,"match_fingerprint":"20b945c1b12b44f7e0991d81616241a739dacb42702f26db27d925baec0e691b","message":"Output size or generation rate is not bounded. Unbounded output enables denial-of-service through resource exhaustion, log flooding, or context-window stuffing.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-a21ec5de7a2d4e708baafa634fd3b503","line":49,"path":"rules/error-handling.md","start_column":26}],"path":"rules/error-handling.md","pattern":"Unbounded Output","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Set explicit limits on output length, generation count, and rate. Use max_tokens and truncation to prevent unbounded output.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"OH3","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":26,"tags":["Output Handling"]},{"category":"Excessive Agency","code_snippet":"\n## Use `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` inside transactions\n\nWhen you dispatch an event inside a database transaction, `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` delays dispatch until all open database transactions commit. If a transaction rolls back, Laravel discards the event. The delay affects synchronous and queued listeners. It is not limited to queue timing.\n\n```php\nclass OrderShipped implements ShouldDispatchAfterCommit {}","confidence":0.7,"evidence":{},"finding":"not limited to","finding_ids":["finding-70703fa280cf4c9ba0465316aa968377"],"id":"sha256:91aaa2b45c9653e49be30db4500dd60c0ba5280d25c6ff9bfa5d81c9da52f1e3","intent":null,"line":16,"match_fingerprint":"943d9aae8743c129fe98eb6cc5e984f5e35ceba0b44ce4ca00f42b97f0bf3eaf","message":"Skill's behavior or capabilities extend beyond its stated purpose. Scope creep allows an agent to perform actions unrelated to its documented functionality, increasing the attack surface.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-70703fa280cf4c9ba0465316aa968377","line":16,"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","start_column":262}],"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","pattern":"Scope Creep","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Limit the skill's scope to its documented purpose. Remove instructions that enable the agent to perform actions outside its stated functionality.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA3","severity":"LOW","start_column":262,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]}],"findings_truncated":false,"freshness":"historical","id":"laravel/boost/laravel-best-practices","kind":"standalone_skill","plugin_path":null,"profile":{"digest":"sha256:a73e7c4a9fa0ac563a885c541d207e90dde2e248ca426f7824cf429d725db921","id":"static-standard-v3"},"raw_finding_count":15,"report_digest":"sha256:8bcdf615b530620a1a316c7e91bb588cf95bbb27440cb55a8a54633fb7ab8748","retry":{"attempt_count":0,"disposition":"none","latest_status":"partial","next_attempt_at":null,"next_profile":null,"reason":"source_or_profile_changed"},"scanned_at":"2026-10-28T12:36:50Z","scanner":{"id":"skillspector","revision":"f3b25697d76256998ca9d42c198d256258d4c035","version":"2.13.1"},"skill_name":"laravel-best-practices","source":{"content_digest":"sha256:e544ab8c76124f2d67ed0263fbef31a3753ca6b772eed43a6902d9166f96881e","path":".ai/laravel/skill/laravel-best-practices","repository":"laravel/boost","revision":"30e24b7c242049e31bd267cd64b57301fc66b2f4"},"status":"partial","target_revision"